  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Kaempferol 3-Neohesperidoside may interact with HL-60 cells through a series of molecular pathways. The compound is identified as a target of multiple metabolites, including [(2S,9R,13R,14S,15R,17R)-14-acetyloxy-16-hydroxy-4-methoxy-2,6,14,17-tetramethyl-3,11-dioxo-10-oxatetracyclo[7.7.1.02,7.013,17]heptadec-4-en-15-yl] acetate, Megastigma-4,6(Z),8(Z)-triene, and (2E)-3-(4-methylphenyl)-N-(2-phenylethyl)prop-2-enamide, all of which are targeted by HL-60 cells. This indicates that Kaempferol 3-Neohesperidoside may exert its biological effects through these metabolites, which in turn interact with HL-60. The evidence suggests a potential role for this compound in modulating cellular processes in HL-60, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The scores from the different paths are consistent, suggesting a general pattern of interaction, but the strength of the evidence varies, with the first path showing the highest confidence.",
